---

Where this came from

Windline is a Windows port of Tendedero (https://github.com/alejandrobujan/tendedero)
by Alejandro Buján. The idea, the design, the geometry and the animations are
his; the Windows implementation is new. Both bodies of work are under the MIT
licence above, and both copyright notices are therefore kept.

---

Name and icon

The MIT License above covers the source code. It does not grant any rights to
the Tendedero name or the Tendedero icon, including the icon artwork drawn by
the original's scripts/make-icon.swift and the images in its docs folder. The
same restriction is restated here because it applies to this work as a modified
version of that one: modified or redistributed versions must use a different name
and a different icon, and must not suggest that they are Tendedero or are endorsed
by its author.

Accordingly this port is called Windline, and its icon is its own: it is not
copied from the original, it is not shipped as opaque artwork, and it is drawn in
code — see drawLogoPrimitives in util.go and the --mkicon mode that renders it to
assets/windline.ico. Referring to Tendedero to say where this work comes from is
expected and welcome; presenting Windline as Tendedero is not.